  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia Ireland Agri food program inception phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Food Systems Ireland (SFSI) is a the government of Ireland agency under the Department of Agriculture, Food and Marine (DAFM). SFSI contracted through one of its five consortium members- Teagasc, is implementing an inception phase for a proposed multi-year Zambia- Ireland Agri-food Programme (ZIAP) with two potential  streams of focus:      1. Dairy sector development, with an emphasisi on the role of diary cooperatives in producer systems formalisation, creation of added value, upskilling of small dairy farmers and improving dairy system efficiency in Zambia                                                                          2. Research and innovation to strengthen sustainable food systems- supporting the delivery of technical knowledge and interventions to help Zambia embark on sustainable food systems transformation pathways</narrative>
  </description>
